XC(1L)            MISC. REFERENCE MANUAL PAGES             XC(1L)NAME     xc, xcb - execute commands contained in a fileSYNOPSIS     xc or xcb [ -c key_character ] [ file ]DESCRIPTION     Xc searches a file for a sequence of lines with the form     %c command_line     or     $c command_line     where 'c' is a single key character given with the  -c  com-     mand  line  option.   It  then executes each command_line in     turn.     If the -c option is omitted, lines with the form     % command_line     or     $ command_line     are executed.  The `%' form echos the command line; the  `$'     form does not.     When invoked as xcb, the program automatically runs  in  the     background,  redirects the standar output and standard error     output to the file ./ERRS, and makes a short announcement on     its controlling terminal when it finishes.     Xc saves the last filename and key character which were used     into  the  file  $HOME/.xc, and uses that file's contents as     the defaults if the file argument is omitted.     If the file contains program source  code,  the  xc  command     lines  should probably be enclosed within comments; however,     the `%' and `$' must be the first characters on their lines,     and be immediately followed by the key characters.FILES     $HOME/.xc     ERRSSEE ALSO     cc(1), sh(1)AUTHOR     David MacKenzie (mostly)Sun Release 4.0           Last change:                          1